# 基础词 Unit17
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-基础词
# 描述: 基础词Unit17核心词汇

{{drown}}{/draʊn/}}v. 溺水；淹没}}{{The heavy rain nearly drowned the small town.}}
{{drug}}{/drʌɡ/}}n. 药物；毒品}}{{The new drug has been approved for clinical use.}}
{{drum}}{/drʌm/}}n. 鼓；桶}}{{The drummer played a精彩的solo at the concert.}}
{{drunk}}{/drʌŋk/}}adj. 醉的；n. 醉汉}}{{It is dangerous to drive when you are drunk.}}
{{dry}}{/draɪ/}}adj. 干的；v. 使干燥}}{{The clothes are dry enough to wear now.}}
{{due}}{/djuː/}}adj. 到期的；应给的；由于}}{{The report is due by the end of this week.}}
{{dull}}{/dʌl/}}adj. 迟钝的；无聊的；阴暗的}}{{The lecture was so dull that many students fell asleep.}}
{{dump}}{/dʌmp/}}v. 倾倒；抛弃；n. 垃圾场}}{{It is illegal to dump waste in the river.}}
{{during}}{/ˈdjʊərɪŋ/}}prep. 在…期间}}{{She read many books during her summer vacation.}}
{{dust}}{/dʌst/}}n. 灰尘；v. 擦去灰尘}}{{There was a thick layer of dust on the old furniture.}}
{{duty}}{/ˈdjuːti/}}n. 责任；义务；税}}{{It is our duty to protect the environment.}}
{{dwell}}{/dwel/}}v. 居住；详述}}{{The old man dwelled in a cottage by the lake.}}
{{dynamic}}{/daɪˈnæmɪk/}}adj. 动态的；有活力的}}{{The city has a dynamic economy that continues to grow.}}
{{each}}{/iːtʃ/}}adj./pron. 每个；各自}}{{Each student received a certificate at the ceremony.}}
{{eager}}{/ˈiːɡər/}}adj. 渴望的；热切的}}{{She is eager to learn about different cultures.}}
{{ear}}{/ɪər/}}n. 耳朵}}{{She has a good ear for music.}}
{{early}}{/ˈɜːrli/}}adj./adv. 早的；提前}}{{She arrived early for the meeting.}}
{{earn}}{/ɜːrn/}}v. 赚得；赢得}}{{He earns a good salary as a software engineer.}}
{{earth}}{/ɜːrθ/}}n. 地球；土地}}{{The earth revolves around the sun once a year.}}
{{ease}}{/iːz/}}n. 容易；舒适；v. 减轻}}{{He solved the problem with ease.}}
{{east}}{/iːst/}}n./adj. 东方（的）}}{{The sun rises in the east every morning.}}
{{easy}}{/ˈiːzi/}}adj. 容易的；轻松的}}{{The exam was easier than I expected.}}
{{eat}}{/iːt/}}v. 吃}}{{We should eat more fruits and vegetables.}}
{{economic}}{/ˌiːkəˈnɒmɪk/}}adj. 经济的；经济学的}}{{The economic situation has improved this year.}}
{{economy}}{/ɪˈkɒnəmi/}}n. 经济；节约}}{{The country's economy is growing rapidly.}}
{{edge}}{/edʒ/}}n. 边缘；优势}}{{She stood at the edge of the cliff looking down.}}
{{edition}}{/ɪˈdɪʃn/}}n. 版；版本}}{{The third edition of the textbook has been updated.}}
{{editor}}{/ˈedɪtər/}}n. 编辑；编者}}{{The editor reviewed the article before publication.}}
{{educate}}{/ˈedʒukeɪt/}}v. 教育；培养}}{{The program aims to educate children about the environment.}}
{{effect}}{/ɪˈfekt/}}n. 效果；影响}}{{The new policy had a positive effect on the economy.}}
{{effective}}{/ɪˈfektɪv/}}adj. 有效的；生效的}}{{Regular exercise is an effective way to reduce stress.}}
{{efficient}}{/ɪˈfɪʃnt/}}adj. 高效的；有效率的}}{{The new system is much more efficient than the old one.}}
{{effort}}{/ˈefərt/}}n. 努力；成就}}{{She put a lot of effort into preparing for the exam.}}
{{egg}}{/eɡ/}}n. 蛋；卵}}{{She had boiled eggs and toast for breakfast.}}
{{either}}{/ˈiːðər/}}adj./pron. 两者之一；adv. 也}}{{You can choose either option; both are good.}}
{{elder}}{/ˈeldər/}}adj. 年长的；n. 长辈}}{{My elder brother is five years older than me.}}
{{elect}}{/ɪˈlekt/}}v. 选举；选择}}{{The people elected a new president last November.}}
{{electric}}{/ɪˈlektrɪk/}}adj. 电的；电动的}}{{The electric car is becoming more popular.}}
{{elegant}}{/ˈelɪɡənt/}}adj. 优雅的；精美的}}{{The ballroom was decorated in an elegant style.}}
{{element}}{/ˈelɪmənt/}}n. 元素；成分；要素}}{{Oxygen is one of the most important elements for life.}}
